 the central work\, Leans\, Reverses (2022)\, emerges from the relationship
  between a dance performance\, its recording\, and transcription (a choreo
 graphic score\, captions\, and audio description). The installation includ
 es t\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-08-16 06:31 PDT
LOCATION:Cantor Arts Center
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Cantor Arts] JANE! An intimate exploration of Gilded Age excess 
  and the enigmatic life and death of Jane Stanford
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260817
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260817
DTSTAMP:20260816T133124Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-52880326677126-52880513718031@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Curated by Associate Curator of European Art\, Patrick R. Crow
 ley\, JANE! celebrates the aesthetic and affective excesses of Jane Stanfo
 rd\, the Gilded Age founder and matriarch of Stanford University. Bringing
  together precious keepsakes\, souvenirs\, archaeological detritus\, and s
 pooky messages from beyond the grave\, the exhibition reveals the campy un
 derside of a familiar biography and perhaps an even more familiar murder m
 ystery.\n\nFrom her elegant French gowns to a colossal painting of her jew
 els\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://museum.stanford.edu/exhibitions/jan
 e\nLast synced: 2026-08-16 06:31 PDT
LOCATION:Cantor Arts Center
URL:https://museum.stanford.edu/exhibitions/jane
END:VEVENT
